{"id":"9a2fb66895acc799","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-generic-absoluteness.md","title":"Generic Absoluteness","display":"thm-generic-absoluteness — Generic Absoluteness","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-generic-absoluteness","aliases":["58-thm-generic-absoluteness","Generic Absoluteness","Shoenfield Absoluteness Extended"],"display":"thm-generic-absoluteness — Generic Absoluteness","depends_on":["[[58-thm-shoenfield]]","[[58-df-ctm]]","[[58-df-poset]]","[[58-df-generic]]","[[58-df-generic-extension]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-generic-absoluteness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-generic-absoluteness</span><span>Generic Absoluteness</span><span>Shoenfield Absoluteness Extended</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-generic-absoluteness — Generic Absoluteness"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"da6e3d3afda6cce6\" href=\"?note=da6e3d3afda6cce6\" title=\"58-thm-shoenfield\">58-thm-shoenfield</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"66d43bb76d055059\" href=\"?note=66d43bb76d055059\" title=\"58-df-ctm\">58-df-ctm</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"58-df-poset\">58-df-poset</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"545853811ce0a4b6\" href=\"?note=545853811ce0a4b6\" title=\"58-df-generic\">58-df-generic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"76dde059f166d3e6\" href=\"?note=76dde059f166d3e6\" title=\"58-df-generic-extension\">58-df-generic-extension</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,\\Gamma,P,\\leq_P,G,N,r,\\varphi\\in V\">\\(M,\\Gamma,P,\\leq_P,G,N,r,\\varphi\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\">\\(\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Poset}(P,\\leq_P)\">\\(\\mathrm{Poset}(P,\\leq_P)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,\\leq_P,M)\">\\(\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,\\leq_P,M)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(N,M,\\Gamma,P,G)\">\\(\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(N,M,\\Gamma,P,G)\\)</span> are the exact setup predicates.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZFC}\\subseteq\\Gamma\">\\(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\subseteq\\Gamma\\)</span> supplies the set theory needed by Shoenfield absoluteness.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\">\\(\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\)</span> means that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\">\\(\\varphi\\)</span> is a coded <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_2\">\\(\\Sigma^1_2\\)</span> formula of second-order arithmetic with real parameter <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r\">\\(r\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span> is the metatheoretic projective-truth relation used in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"da6e3d3afda6cce6\" href=\"?note=da6e3d3afda6cce6\" title=\"58-thm-shoenfield\">58-thm-shoenfield</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}generic\\text{-}absoluteness}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land\\mathrm{ZFC}\\subseteq\\Gamma\n\\land P,\\leq_P\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P,\\leq_P)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,\\leq_P,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(N,M,\\Gamma,P,G)\n\\land r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\n\\land\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\longrightarrow\\left(\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\varphi,r)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(N,\\varphi,r)\n\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}generic\\text{-}absoluteness}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land\\mathrm{ZFC}\\subseteq\\Gamma\n\\land P,\\leq_P\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P,\\leq_P)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,\\leq_P,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(N,M,\\Gamma,P,G)\n\\land r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\n\\land\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\longrightarrow\\left(\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\varphi,r)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(N,\\varphi,r)\n\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Shoenfield (1961): proved <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_2/\\Pi^1_2\">\\(\\Sigma^1_2/\\Pi^1_2\\)</span> absoluteness.</li>\n<li>The complexity restriction to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_2\">\\(\\Sigma^1_2\\)</span> (and dually <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Pi^1_2\">\\(\\Pi^1_2\\)</span>) is essential for Shoenfield absoluteness.</li>\n<li>The theory parameter is retained in the five-place generic-extension relation and is required to contain ZFC; the former four-place projection could choose an unrelated hidden theory.</li>\n<li>Forcing invariance can be restated via the forcing relation in the ground model.</li>\n<li>Stronger absoluteness principles typically require forcing axioms or large cardinals.</li>\n<li>Applications: understanding independence limits.</li>\n<li>Higher absoluteness: requires stronger forcing axioms or large cardinals.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-thm-shoenfield","status":"resolved","id":"da6e3d3afda6cce6","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-thm-shoenfield]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ctm","status":"resolved","id":"66d43bb76d055059","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-ctm]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-poset","status":"resolved","id":"d3f859dbdd37f018","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-poset]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-generic","status":"resolved","id":"545853811ce0a4b6","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-generic]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-generic-extension","status":"resolved","id":"76dde059f166d3e6","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-generic-extension]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-thm-shoenfield","status":"resolved","id":"da6e3d3afda6cce6","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}$ is the metatheoretic projective-truth relation used in [[58-thm-shoenfield]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M,\\Gamma,P,\\leq_P,G,N,r,\\varphi\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Poset}(P,\\leq_P)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,\\leq_P,M)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(N,M,\\Gamma,P,G)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZFC}\\subseteq\\Gamma","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma^1_2","display":false},{"tex":"r","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}generic\\text{-}absoluteness}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land\\mathrm{ZFC}\\subseteq\\Gamma\n\\land P,\\leq_P\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P,\\leq_P)\\\\\n&\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,\\leq_P,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(N,M,\\Gamma,P,G)\n\\land r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\n\\land\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\\\\n&\\quad\\longrightarrow\\left(\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\varphi,r)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(N,\\varphi,r)\n\\right).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\Sigma^1_2/\\Pi^1_2","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma^1_2","display":false},{"tex":"\\Pi^1_2","display":false}],"bytes":2240,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4175","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-thm-generic-absoluteness.md|58-thm-generic-absoluteness]]（batch20）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-188","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-extension.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-is-transitive.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-ZFC.md]]\n[[58-thm-MM.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equal-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equals-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-absoluteness-calculation.md]]\n[[58-thm-ac-wellorder-equivalent.md]]\n[[58-thm-aleph-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-completeness.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-set-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category-theory.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category.md]]\n[[58-thm-banach-tarski.md]]\n[[58-thm-beth-function-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-boolean-valued-model.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-cardinality.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-determinacy-proof.md]]\n[[58-thm-bounded-forcing-axioms.md]]\n[[58-thm-cantor.md]]\n[[58-thm-cardinal-multiplication.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-filter-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-guessing.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-intersection-proper.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-i